    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Coriolis force is zero at the Equator; hence, tropical cyclones do not form within 0° to 5° latitude.",
        "In the Northern Hemisphere, cyclone winds rotate counter-clockwise, whereas anticyclones rotate clockwise.",
        "Tropical cyclones travel generally from East to West driven by Trade Winds, whereas Temperate cyclones move West to East under Westerlies.",
        "Fronts are exclusively associated with Temperate (Extra-Tropical) Cyclones and are completely absent in Tropical Cyclones."
      ],
      "id": "p09pqje"
